1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,000
This is equipe: a squad of AI coding agents that works like a team —

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
a PM, engineers, a board of tickets, and you accepting the work.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,500
I ask the PM for a small change. It writes a ticket with acceptance criteria

4
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:29,500
and hands it to an engineer, who works on its own git branch, in its own worktree,

5
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:38,000
so my checkout is never touched.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:46,000
When the work is done, the engineer hands it in.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Until now, the only one who had read this code was the agent that wrote it.

8
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:07,000
So every hand-in now goes to an NVIDIA Nemotron model on Nebius Token Factory.

9
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:16,000
It reads the diff against the ticket and comes back with a verdict, a short summary,

10
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:25,000
risks with the file and line, and the tests the change is missing —

11
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:32,000
in my language.

12
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:41,000
It's advice, not authority: the review goes on the ticket's record, and I still decide —

13
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:50,000
here I send it back with the risk it found.

14
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:58,000
You don't need the whole squad to try it. With only a Nebius key,

15
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:08,000
equipe review lists the account's Nemotron models and reviews any git repository's changes —

16
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:16,000
same client, real tokens, real request id.

17
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Under the hood it's one small Rust client: an OpenAI-compatible chat completion to Token Factory.

18
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:30,000
The diff is treated as data, not instructions; the answer must be one bounded JSON review,

19
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
or it's rejected — never made up. The key stays in the environment and never reaches the logs.

20
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,000
equipe is open source under MIT.

21
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,000
A team of agents, and a second pair of eyes from NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius.
